WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.011
In analytical modeling the grain question remains

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:08.003
essential A fact table represents measurable events

00:00:08.913 --> 00:00:11.453
Before adding columns state exactly what one

00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:15.499
fact row means A star schema connects

00:00:15.525 --> 00:00:18.223
the fact table directly to descriptive dimensions

00:00:19.146 --> 00:00:21.883
This often makes analytical queries easier to

00:00:21.909 --> 00:00:27.061
understand A snowflake design normalizes some
dimensions

00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:31.208
into related sub-dimensions That can reduce
redundancy

00:00:31.221 --> 00:00:35.252
but increases the number of joins Neither

00:00:35.279 --> 00:00:37.489
pattern removes the need to define grain

00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:41.915
For our clinic example one possible fact

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.431
grain is one appointment-service line That sentence

00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:47.365
tells us what each fact row represents

00:00:47.378 --> 00:00:49.681
and which measures keys and dimensions can

00:00:49.694 --> 00:00:54.001
belong there Always define fact grain before

00:00:54.015 --> 00:00:55.817
designing an analytical table
